    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d399-a2">

                <pb facs="0763" n="653" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg653"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No.
                    387.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Azpiroz to Mr. Ryan.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-08-18"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 18,
                        1890</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: As I had the honor to advise Your
                    Excellency in our interview of the 16th instant, I to-day advised the President
                    of the instructions which the Government of the United States had conveyed to
                    its representative in Central America, in accordance with the copy Your
                    Excellency was pleased to deliver to me; and I have the satisfaction to inform
                    you that, in accordance with the decision of the President, instructions
                    identical thereto are being transmitted to our chargé d’ affaires in
                    Guatemala.</p>
                <p>It gratifies me, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">M. Azpiroz.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
